+# X-027 test record for the EngineAccessPlan patches (branch eap-x290)
+
+Valid results are those at 6a4cd0f with this worktree's own target directory (reth/reth-2.9.0-eap/target),
+2026-11-02 13:4x, `scripts/x290_cargo.sh` under labq heavy:
+
+- `cargo test --release -p evm2 -p evm2-jit-builtins -p evm2-jit-runtime --features evm2-jit-runtime/llvm --lib`:
+  evm2 719/719, evm2-jit-builtins 7/7, evm2-jit-runtime 112/113; the failure is a JIT-memory accounting test
+  (jit_memory_tracks_compilation; eviction_frees_jit_memory in another run) that also fails on unpatched f93318f
+  in a parallel run and passes single-threaded on the patched tree.
+- Single-threaded: compiled_keccak_and_balance_reads_reach_thread_hooks, inspector_allowing_compiled_frames_keeps_message_hooks,
+  eviction_frees_jit_memory, jit_memory_tracks_compilation, unobserved_lookup_on_blocking_backend_does_not_compile,
+  unobserved_lookups_neither_count_nor_compile: 6/6 pass.
+
+Void: one run in which an unpatched f93318f worktree shared the target directory; cargo hashes path crates without
+their path, so that build overwrote the patched evm2 artifacts and the run compiled the patched tests against the
+unpatched evm2 (it failed to compile). Its result is not used.
